>Hypothermia quick card
Suspect hypothermia? Call emergency services (UK: 999).

After cold exposure, look for shivering, slurred speech, confusion, drowsiness or slow breathing.
Shelter gently. Remove wet clothing once sheltered and wrap in dry layers. Insulate from the ground. Stay and monitor breathing.
No hot bath, direct heat, rubbing or alcohol. If unresponsive and not breathing normally, start CPR and follow the dispatcher.

